Mrs. Elnora Stevens, her son played football with Richard, so she took me under her wing.

2638
01:41:25.045 --> 01:41:27.061
I tell you what that lady did.

2639
01:41:27.061 --> 01:41:29.939
We had just moved, in the first house in ’73 . . .

2640
01:41:29.939 --> 01:41:30.803
<v ARSENEAULT>On Prater Road?

2641
01:41:30.803 --> 01:41:32.818
<v LEE>She came . . . On Prater Road in ’73.

2642
01:41:32.818 --> 01:41:39.727
She came with her mop and her bucket and she mopped . . . You know like those vinyl floors still have the name written on them?

2643
01:41:39.727 --> 01:41:43.470
She mopped all of the floors and then she just left like that.

2644
01:41:43.470 --> 01:41:46.061
It was like . . . Those people were like awesome, guys.

2645
01:41:46.061 --> 01:41:46.924
They were awesome.

2646
01:41:46.924 --> 01:41:47.788
They were awesome.

2647
01:41:47.788 --> 01:41:51.818
And that’s why Mossville was such a close knit . . . because people loved each other.

2648
01:41:51.818 --> 01:41:54.409
They respected each other, they cared for each other.

2649
01:41:54.409 --> 01:41:55.561
Just like in Jeanerette.

2650
01:41:55.561 --> 01:42:01.606
If something happened down the street your parents knew about it before you got home and it was the same thing.

2651
01:42:01.606 --> 01:42:08.803
A village . . . a community raising a child is what . . . And so Ms. Flo next door to me had the same amount of land as we.

2652
01:42:08.803 --> 01:42:09.379
Three acres.

2653
01:42:09.379 --> 01:42:11.682
She and her mom, Ms. Pearl . . . Sweet people.

2654
01:42:11.682 --> 01:42:12.833
Loved their little garden.

2655
01:42:12.833 --> 01:42:19.455
They planted out in the garden, they worked in the yard and I would work in my yard, she would work in hers.

2656
01:42:19.455 --> 01:42:21.758
She say, “T you ready to go in?”

2657
01:42:21.758 --> 01:42:22.909
I’d say, “Not quite.”

2658
01:42:22.909 --> 01:42:23.773
She said, “Okay.”

2659
01:42:23.773 --> 01:42:29.818
She would stay in her yard until it was time for me to go in so we would go in together.

2660
01:42:29.818 --> 01:42:33.561
And I tell you, the year I retired in 2003 I missed her.

2661
01:42:33.561 --> 01:42:39.030
It was like I’d gone out and I said, “Where’s Ms. Flo Rich?” he said, “I haven’t seen her.”

2662
01:42:39.030 --> 01:42:40.470
And it was that Friday.

2663
01:42:40.470 --> 01:42:42.485
And Saturday I still didn’t see her.

2664
01:42:42.485 --> 01:42:43.924
I said something’s not right.

2665
01:42:43.924 --> 01:42:46.515
Saturday morning guys, I went and I walked over.

2666
01:42:46.515 --> 01:42:50.545
And when I touched her screen door, it was locked from the inside out.

2667
01:42:50.545 --> 01:42:52.561
I said, “Oh my God something’s wrong.”

2668
01:42:52.561 --> 01:42:54.000
And she had passed . . .

2669
01:42:54.000 --> 01:42:54.881
<v HOLMAN>In her sleep.

2670
01:42:54.881 --> 01:42:55.761
<v LEE>In her sleep.

2671
01:42:55.761 --> 01:42:56.055
<v ARSENEAULT>Wow.

2672
01:42:56.055 --> 01:42:56.936
